{:id "0032-lab-steady-line"
 :title "Lab: the line holds still while you type, and words move in depth, not into their neighbours"
 :lupa/deps #{"0031-lab-debug"}
 :lupa/area :lab
 :lupa/risk :medium
 :goal "Ben's first screen recording on his M5 (WebGPU, 33.6 s, read frame
        by frame by the foreman; docs/sample-media) shows two problems the
        tests could not. (1) The whole line slides left as he types: the
        renderer centres the text block on its live extent, so every new
        letter shifts everything by half its advance (\"This\" drifted about
        60 px in two seconds). Typing into a moving target. (2) :fuse
        spreads a word's letters sideways so far that they collide with the
        previous word and jump past the caret (\"am e r g |e\"). Fix both:
        a steady writing surface, and effects that use depth and height
        rather than invading the neighbours' space."
 :scope ["src/halfahead/lab/pose.cljc" "test/halfahead/lab/pose_test.cljc"
         "src/halfahead/lab/render.cljs" "src/halfahead/lab/main.cljs"
         "e2e/lab.mjs" "docs/LAB.md"]
 :design "Steady surface (render.cljs, main.cljs): lay text out in a column
          of fixed width (the width-em main.cljs already chooses), and centre
          the COLUMN on the stage, not the text's live extent. Text is
          left-aligned within the column, like a page, so a line grows to
          the right and never moves while you type. The camera stays on the
          column's centre (the lean check keeps passing). Vertically, the
          block may still ease upward as lines are added (one move per new
          line, eased, never per keystroke).
          Contained effects (pose.cljc): horizontal displacement of a cued
          glyph must stay within half an em of its base x at all times for
          every effect, so a word never reaches its neighbours. :fuse
          becomes a convergence in depth and height: letters start spread
          in z (toward the camera) and slightly in y, alternating by
          position, and converge to the line; :skitter and :jitter keep
          their x motion inside the same bound. All existing properties
          (valid frame, letters spell the draft, settling, reduced motion)
          keep holding.
          e2e/lab.mjs: a step that types \"This is a merge of a \" at 70 ms
          per key and samples the base-layout x of the first glyph's
          projected position every 100 ms while typing: it may not move by
          more than 2 px (the line holds still); and a step asserting that
          during the :fuse of \"merge\" no glyph of \"merge\" is ever
          projected left of the right edge of the preceding \"a\".
          docs/LAB.md: a line on the steady surface and contained effects."
 :acceptance
 ["Property: for every effect, at every time, every cued glyph's |x - base
   x| <= 0.5 em (new test over generated drafts and times)"
  "All existing pose properties still pass"
  "`bb lab:e2e` passes with the two new steps; the final message lists the
   screenshots (the foreman will look at them)"
  "`bb test` stays green"]
 :non-goals
 ["Do not edit the schema, lab.draft, lab.cues, or the glossary"
  "No new effects; do not run `bb e2e` or `bb play`"]
 :context ["src/halfahead/lab/pose.cljc" "src/halfahead/lab/render.cljs"
           "src/halfahead/lab/main.cljs" "e2e/lab.mjs" "docs/LAB.md"]
 :budget-usd 10.0}
